{"title":"1972 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(very_long,_but_detailed)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (very long, but detailed)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Venn_Diagram)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Venn Diagram)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The symbols <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3eff218e72b51ce01e4e22f8b5d0de73e89c34e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,\\ldots,g)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a435cfa873528fda8011ab1fee0f179f1233b4d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b,\\ldots, g]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> denote the greatest common divisor and least common multiple, respectively, of the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a86d179d0b1dfa5c2e9da13f569f422d853b818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,\\ldots, g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a3ba14719de565e9b2cc5dbbc6b53efc413927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,6,18)=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce61f21da055164e6c4aa95b4ac1c682bb8075a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[6,15]=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a3797d87dfc7855e74fd6a01e4f48819256cecb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[a,b,c]^2}{[a,b][b,c][c,a]}=\\frac{(a,b,c)^2}{(a,b)(b,c)(c,a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"256\" height=\"45\" />.</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider an arbitrary prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b293939f84e9150b56a9f84510d042d08ded77b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56ff45a03c5a46c043a5b70209ec62fd35e7da96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af859774dc4e78d798a47c8b1c4afb292adeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> be the greatest powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. \nWLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed40802461858d573195c79ed5cc089988ceb08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha \\leq \\beta \\leq \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Examining each factor in the equation, we see that the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that divides the left hand side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e7908df4625bfa84dd687576bdc69cf2a2ac0bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\gamma -(\\beta+\\gamma+\\gamma) = -\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />, and the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that divides the right hand side is 2\\alpha -(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59bc6cad81d3dd45f01425ab9623cf717c28d5f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta + \\alpha) = -\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />. Since every prime has the same power in both expressions, the expressions are equal. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1ba54b51ae6ec573d9ad4dc3479d5389803529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = (a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13ca6f75d7d45a4f133c194e89362b1408274fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq = (a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/0192c4cbedcc60fb8208b38456e19f78fc89888f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pr = (b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ae0e502dba08cbc48b6e8fb282ff37413f9c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ps = (c, a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. Then it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3b250cbe748b0276e4acf1d9b3b3d8c86809d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q, r, s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" /> are pairwise coprime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4bb930ca971a353194046637285a76552071f08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = pqsa&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c2c28b16f9f8f43d09a82c7b714503a06ad3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = pqrb&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2bd7b8ceaafcaa79c19b718bd898d9b31f0d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = prsc&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81b003fecce1b1eab902c91f0ef019d0d2183b15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;, b&#39;, c&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> pairwise coprime as well. Then, we wish to show\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/2491c95b0cc5cd29d2ae08db82523d8688299193.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(pqrsa&#39;b&#39;c&#39;)^2}{(pqrsa&#39;b&#39;)(pqrsb&#39;c&#39;)(pqrsc&#39;a&#39;)} = \\frac{p^2}{(pq)(pr)(ps)},\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"43\" />\nwhich can be checked fairly easily.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28very_long.2C_but_detailed.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(very_long,_but_detailed)\">Solution 3 (very long, but detailed)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (very long, but detailed)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note: This solution is more of a \"bashy\" solution, and is easier to think of than the first 2 solutions.\n</p><p>Dividing both sides of the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc39262e4de40e74ca0e405f3a1f8689248d8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" />, and then multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7b677dd4ac7df3aa1dcc41eb90258e07bc4b95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b][b,c][c,a]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e7637595e9543dad1fe9ee8ece0f7bcf196d23f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{[a,b,c]}{(a,b,c)}\\right)^2 = \\frac{[a,b][b,c][c,a]}{(a,b)(b,c)(c,a)}.\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"46\" />\nNow, we look at the prime factorisations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Let \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/406a14c4d1224e8c7f0e18e96533a35e86455d98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=2^{x_1}\\cdot 3^{x_2}\\cdot 5^{x_3}\\cdots,\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab8dd65cf28ad137ec93578feedf5ea00e1a965.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b=2^{y_1}\\cdot 3^{y_2}\\cdot 5^{y_3}\\cdots,\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe89a02cf3397e9da5f8bbd92a66c0341d10dfe1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c=2^{z_1}\\cdot 3^{z_2}\\cdot 5^{z_3}\\cdots,\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" />\nwhere all of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0eebd00c02420b72303b8c5f521965fe6456258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, y_1, z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"11\" /> are nonnegative integers (they could be 0).\nThus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/9299678a08e293913a53e519d8614c2ea5c20fcb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[a,b,c]=2^{\\max(x_1,y_1,z_1)} \\cdot 3^{\\max(x_2,y_2,z_2)} \\cdot 5^{\\max(x_3,y_3,z_3)} \\cdots\\]\" width=\"401\" height=\"21\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126ff662581157583cc7be362062a5f2aaca6ce6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a,b,c)=2^{\\min(x_1,y_1,z_1)} \\cdot 3^{\\min(x_2,y_2,z_2)} \\cdot 5^{\\min(x_3,y_3,z_3)} \\cdots.\\]\" width=\"409\" height=\"20\" />\nNow, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a70a363977f0965fb8c571218d1b27c8c5c0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{[a,b,c]}{(a,b,c)}\\right) = 2^{\\max(x_1,y_1,z_1) - \\min(x_1,y_1,z_1)} \\cdot 3^{\\max(x_2,y_2,z_2) - \\min(x_2,y_2,z_2)} \\cdot 5^{\\max(x_3,y_3,z_3) - \\min(x_3,y_3,z_3)} \\cdots.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"724\" height=\"45\" /> Squaring the LHS will just double all the exponents on the RHS.\n</p><p><br />\nAlso, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d6008380fc38277fe9fdccd9c125e166c77bf5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]=2^{\\max(x_1,y_1)} \\cdot 3^{\\max(x_2,y_2)} \\cdot 5^{\\max(x_3,y_3)} \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"336\" height=\"21\" />. We can also build similar equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb5fa06b68f7db4cd6ad9ac6fe7d647c906cb11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[b,c],[c,a],(a,b),(b,c)(c,a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" />, using 2 of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> and either the minimum of the exponents or the maximum.\nWe see that when we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bcc73f1c5fc7841137eafa2907c5e05eab3fc387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[b,c]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69c612110d0ded2743d8a8cec2a4fca89d4fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,c]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> together, the exponents of the prime factorization will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c669471169fdd1c12ad26e6e1cd9bc70eb11e39f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(x_i,y_i)+ \\max(y_i,z_i)+ \\max(z_i,x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"301\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />'th prime. \nWhen we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fe40b98e74737c70752abaa29332bc3369bfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a53387373f79f3f15a70abeeb58639c7d60aa2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> together, the exponents of the prime factorization will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb30d7a26a52720d28c861bfcf171da807b7a7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(x_i,y_i)+ \\min(y_i,z_i)+ \\min(z_i,x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"291\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />'th prime.\n</p><p>Thus, when we divide the former by the latter, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/53272794a5e710fd33efd9dc1685bc1b1a09777f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(x_i,y_i)+ \\max(y_i,z_i)+ \\max(x_i,z_i) - (\\min(x_i,y_i)+ \\min(y_i,z_i)+ \\min(x_i,z_i))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"626\" height=\"18\" />. We wish to prove that this is equal to the exponents we got from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0ca7677b3818f3640562118c9b9a1b486262592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$([a,b,c]/(a,b,c))^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>In other words, this problem is now down to proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/8464fb0c85cf1bf7c020b406af5740b6455bf601.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(\\max(x_i,y_i,z_i) - \\min(x_i,y_i,z_i)) = \\max(x_i,y_i)+ \\max(y_i,z_i)+ \\max(x_i,z_i) - (\\min(x_i,y_i)+ \\min(y_i,z_i)+ \\min(x_i,z_i))\\]\" width=\"861\" height=\"18\" /> for any nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd603edbc842300d7a1122fd905197c6dc7235a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i, y_i, z_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" />. WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26ae7e8772afc9da95300002083d585403472e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i \\le y_i \\le z_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, computing maximums and minimums, this equation turns into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fca28bbd4b4936e5a9af4e29e207b31f6a121c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(z_i - x_i) = y_i + z_i + z_i - x_i - y_i - x_i.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Finally, canceling out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />'s and collecting like terms, we see the RHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc9117a7d459ed65e0218f8ebcc8037826fe5886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2z_i - 2x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />, which is equal to the LHS. Thus, this equation is true, and we are done. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4fe87cadde69d85944a1b38cc4a51965b03ee40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=dzxA\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3f1dc378aaacabcf5b2f6ef1c3f93f32e573eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b=dxyB\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e45bb8b20e516e727f4e8fc4130ce95631136d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c=dyzC\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd003eff1a32e89ac6975ed7e4cbb875fce4788e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(A,B,C)=\\gcd(x,y,z)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />. (Existence proof missing.) Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a7bc5ff99070fe7361c6a20c0f999d945336fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{lcm}(a,b,c)^2=(dxyzABC)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a7893abbc76979d36ab39dd050c3583360f8cfec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{lcm}(a,b)=dxyzAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. Using this cyclically, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3b6672099aa3e1419f39c6bc8b2df9a147a87c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{LHS}=\\frac{d^2x^2y^2z^2A^2B^2C^2}{(dxyzAB)(dxyzBC)(dxyzCA)}=\\frac{1}{dxyz}.\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"43\" />Now, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/75239cbfd21c627302856b05b1c033c4c5bb7f7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a,b,c)^2=d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d7cd7dba9a4dd0bf3aa250c9bb2aa5b2197a51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a,b)=dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />. Using this cyclically, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d449b86c3948647dcf237dc3485fabacaa9f251.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{RHS}=\\frac{d^2}{(dx)(dy)(dz)}=\\frac{1}{dxyz}.\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"43\" />\n-brainiacmaniac31\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If one thinks of the problem from a set theory vantage point, it is quite intuitive to recognize from PIE:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acdf5e646d8ff564c5c7cc42570e79dc8e5a6b45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{lcm}(a,b,c) = \\frac{a \\cdot b \\cdot c \\cdot \\text{gcd}(a,b,c)}{\\text{gcd}(a,b) \\cdot \\text{gcd}(b,c) \\cdot \\text{gcd}(c,a)}\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"43\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a7f84b90c7b7a944400be375cb8adeb7e73183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{lcm}(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> can be thought of as the union, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f777f920f013580b189e2621f8fecbf04d5c34de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\cdot b \\cdot c$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> can be thought of as the raw addition of sets, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/90532c5e1e39f45c92592c869e856d05ae869465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> function can be thought of as intersections. \n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Venn_Diagram.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Venn_Diagram)\">Video Solution (Venn Diagram)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Venn Diagram)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SisNWPQw_S4\">https://youtu.be/SisNWPQw_S4</a>\n-radlad5\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO\" title=\"1972 USAMO\">1972 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1972 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1972\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1972 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1972 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1972 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1972 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1972 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016222334\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 457/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1588/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15286/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.355      1 -total\n 39.03%    6.774      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 31.61%    5.485      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 27.88%    4.838      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7525:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016222334 and revision id 258172. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}